<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert !c.isEmpty() => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

However, since we need to compare the entire list to the collection, a more appropriate assert statement would be:

<code>assert this.size() == c.size() && (\forall int i; 0 <= i && i < c.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]));</code>

This ensures that the list size matches the collection size and that each element in the list corresponds to the element at the same index in the collection.
